11. Conclusion
The Farmer Crop Selling Management System demonstrates a practical use of MySQL for crop sales record management. It combines relational tables, constraints, joins, aggregate queries, a view, a stored procedure, and triggers to support consistent data storage and useful reports. The project provides a beginner-friendly example of applying DBMS concepts to an agricultural use case.
